1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,795
This is HeadLog, a headache diary for Android.

2
00:00:04,095 --> 00:00:07,892
It makes it easy to track your headaches, and what triggers or eases them.

3
00:00:08,192 --> 00:00:09,621
Let's look around first.

4
00:00:09,921 --> 00:00:11,649
Installation follows at the end.

5
00:00:12,249 --> 00:00:16,708
To see every screen filled, load the demo data under Settings, Advanced.

6
00:00:17,008 --> 00:00:20,272
It fills HeadLog with ninety days of example entries.

7
00:00:20,572 --> 00:00:23,324
You remove them again before you start your own diary.

8
00:00:23,924 --> 00:00:25,299
Today is your home screen:

9
00:00:25,549 --> 00:00:27,690
last night's sleep and the forecast at the top,

10
00:00:27,940 --> 00:00:31,732
then the Headache started button, your drinks and your medication.

11
00:00:32,332 --> 00:00:34,615
When a headache starts, one tap logs it.

12
00:00:34,915 --> 00:00:38,989
Set the intensity, from one to ten, and tap the medication you took.

13
00:00:39,289 --> 00:00:41,316
When it is over, tap Headache is gone.

14
00:00:41,916 --> 00:00:43,729
Only the essentials in the moment.

15
00:00:44,029 --> 00:00:45,437
The details can wait.

16
00:00:45,737 --> 00:00:50,196
Later, tap the headache in today's log, and add symptoms, triggers and a note.

17
00:00:50,796 --> 00:00:52,439
Logging a drink is one tap.

18
00:00:52,739 --> 00:00:55,003
The bar fills up towards your hydration goal,

19
00:00:55,253 --> 00:00:58,051
and the flame counts the days in a row you reached it.

20
00:00:58,651 --> 00:01:01,083
The circle next to the date is the forecast.

21
00:01:01,383 --> 00:01:02,577
Tap it to see why.

22
00:01:02,877 --> 00:01:04,003
It checks five things:

23
00:01:04,253 --> 00:01:06,935
a pressure drop, too little to drink, a short night,

24
00:01:07,185 --> 00:01:09,213
alcohol, and less caffeine than usual.

25
00:01:09,513 --> 00:01:11,689
If none counts against you, it is green.

26
00:01:11,989 --> 00:01:14,357
One makes it yellow, two or more make it red.

27
00:01:14,957 --> 00:01:17,453
Sleep is estimated from your screen activity.

28
00:01:17,753 --> 00:01:20,079
Each morning, HeadLog asks how you slept.

29
00:01:20,379 --> 00:01:22,747
Tap Correct, and the sleep editor opens.

30
00:01:23,347 --> 00:01:26,099
Drag the dots to move falling asleep and waking up.

31
00:01:26,399 --> 00:01:29,748
Tap a wake break to see it magnified, and move its edges.

32
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:31,669
Save, and the night is done.

33
00:01:32,269 --> 00:01:35,832
An hour after your medication, HeadLog asks whether it helped.

34
00:01:36,132 --> 00:01:39,119
Answer No, A bit or Yes, right in the notification.

35
00:01:39,719 --> 00:01:42,791
During a headache, it also asks whether it is still there.

36
00:01:43,091 --> 00:01:44,499
Tap Still there, or Gone.

37
00:01:45,099 --> 00:01:48,495
Through the day, the reminders you switch on arrive the same way:

38
00:01:48,745 --> 00:01:50,211
at noon when you are behind,

39
00:01:50,461 --> 00:01:53,525
and at your check-in times with your drinks as buttons.

40
00:01:54,125 --> 00:01:57,481
In the evening, HeadLog warns you when tomorrow looks risky:

41
00:01:57,731 --> 00:02:01,891
a pressure drop tomorrow, too little to drink today, or alcohol today.

42
00:02:02,491 --> 00:02:03,557
Swipe to Meds.

43
00:02:03,857 --> 00:02:06,494
The gauge counts your medication days in the last thirty,

44
00:02:06,744 --> 00:02:09,383
against the 10/20 rule: at most ten.

45
00:02:09,683 --> 00:02:13,672
Below are your personal limits, and how well each medication worked.

46
00:02:14,272 --> 00:02:16,544
The calendar shows each day at a glance:

47
00:02:16,794 --> 00:02:18,921
headaches, medication as coloured dots,

48
00:02:19,171 --> 00:02:21,931
and a blue line when you reached your hydration goal.

49
00:02:22,231 --> 00:02:23,703
Tap a day for the details.

50
00:02:24,303 --> 00:02:28,164
Insights puts your headaches next to sleep, hydration and air pressure.

51
00:02:28,464 --> 00:02:31,685
Tap or drag across a chart to see the values of a day.

52
00:02:32,285 --> 00:02:35,677
Pick three or seven days, and the timeline goes hour by hour.

53
00:02:35,977 --> 00:02:38,921
It even runs on into tomorrow's pressure forecast.

54
00:02:39,521 --> 00:02:43,231
Headache days compared shows what was different the day before your headaches,

55
00:02:43,481 --> 00:02:44,791
next to the days without.

56
00:02:45,091 --> 00:02:46,648
These are patterns, not proof.

57
00:02:47,248 --> 00:02:48,395
At the top of Insights,

58
00:02:48,645 --> 00:02:52,901
PDF report for your doctor makes one page to take to your appointment.

59
00:02:53,501 --> 00:02:56,336
Your diary lives only on your phone, so back it up:

60
00:02:56,586 --> 00:03:01,160
as a file, or automatically to a secret gist in your GitHub account.

61
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:03,147
Ready for your own diary?

62
00:03:03,447 --> 00:03:07,564
Under Settings, Advanced, Delete all data removes the examples.

63
00:03:07,864 --> 00:03:10,209
HeadLog starts fresh, with three steps:

64
00:03:10,459 --> 00:03:14,157
your medication, your drinks, and extras like sleep and reminders.

65
00:03:14,757 --> 00:03:16,187
Start with your medication.

66
00:03:16,487 --> 00:03:19,751
Tap the pencil next to Medication, then Add medication.

67
00:03:20,051 --> 00:03:21,608
Type the name and the dose.

68
00:03:21,908 --> 00:03:24,916
HeadLog recognises Rizatriptan as a triptan.

69
00:03:25,216 --> 00:03:28,437
Set a personal limit if you like, here four days in thirty.

70
00:03:29,037 --> 00:03:30,083
Then your drinks.

71
00:03:30,383 --> 00:03:33,604
Set your daily hydration goal, here two and a half litres.

72
00:03:33,904 --> 00:03:35,675
Coffee and tea carry their caffeine.

73
00:03:35,975 --> 00:03:40,647
A beer is marked as alcohol, so it counts in the forecast, but not toward your goal.

74
00:03:41,247 --> 00:03:44,852
Reminders are optional, and each one can be changed or turned off.

75
00:03:45,152 --> 00:03:49,120
Here, HeadLog asks every hour during a headache whether it is still there.

76
00:03:49,420 --> 00:03:53,857
It asks at set times what you drank, and reminds you when you are behind your goal.

77
00:03:54,457 --> 00:03:57,977
For the sleep estimate, tick Estimate sleep from screen activity.

78
00:03:58,277 --> 00:04:01,541
Android asks you once to allow usage access for HeadLog.

79
00:04:02,141 --> 00:04:03,443
Now the installation.

80
00:04:03,743 --> 00:04:05,641
HeadLog is not in the Play Store.

81
00:04:05,941 --> 00:04:07,396
You install it with Obtainium,

82
00:04:07,646 --> 00:04:11,019
a free app that installs and updates apps straight from GitHub.

83
00:04:11,319 --> 00:04:14,071
Get it from obtainium.imranr.dev.

84
00:04:14,671 --> 00:04:16,271
In Obtainium, tap Add.

85
00:04:16,571 --> 00:04:22,501
Type the address, github.com/tillraab/headlog, and tap the plus next to it.

86
00:04:23,101 --> 00:04:25,256
Obtainium finds the latest release.

87
00:04:25,556 --> 00:04:27,113
Tap Install, and confirm.

88
00:04:27,413 --> 00:04:30,613
From now on, Obtainium tells you when there is an update.

89
00:04:30,913 --> 00:04:33,111
Then open HeadLog from your home screen.

90
00:04:33,711 --> 00:04:35,908
Free and open source, with no account.

91
00:04:36,208 --> 00:04:37,253
That's HeadLog.
